  "models": {
    "leave": "The higher-priority Leave skill becomes ready120s after this deployment, ignores silence, commits once when the owner is visible and free of intrinsic action control, interrupts an older lock, applies the native Die-to-Leave alias and invokes the normal instant-kill path without marking a route exit. Its zero LP value comes from the canonical record. Cooldown readiness runs in real time; preemption/control scheduling is an explicit shared-engine mapping.",
    "theft": "The LockDamage buff uses serialized event61, independently corroborated as ON_BEFORE_TARGET_APPLY_MODIFIER. A genuine accepted source-owned modifier receipt triggers StealAtk on that modifier recipient while the lock remains affecting. Shield absorption or zero HP damage does not suppress theft. Protected, cancelled, missed or fabricated receipts cannot grant it. Each source retains its gain when a victim leaves, targets keep at least1ATK, the source caps at2050 and overlapping target reductions use strongest-source fallback. Retirement and deployment-life guards clear owned target contributions.",
    "shield": "The permanent shield starts from positive max-HP dynamic state. Physical/Arts incoming raw packets below1200 are cancelled; a qualifying packet resets that state and removes its DEF/RES presentation contribution. The native0.03s refresh is mapped to immediate shared-engine state. Pollution may force GetShield only while no skill is affecting. Retired deployments cannot restore the shield.",
    "transport": "Ordinary speed8 ten-second Arts splash samples current same-life ATK and current selectable bodies at impact, with target/source life guards. A source-object replacement uses the captured birth-deployment view. The speed10 linked skill retains its original target and produces one-second pulses for7s in real time, interrupting on target invalidation, source control/forced silence or retirement. The original shared attack clocks remain a local mapping rather than compiled/frame parity.",
    "limits": "Numeric callback aliases are source facts; accepted/protected/missed receipt ordering, native skill priority/preemption, shield refresh, collider geometry and ordinary/channel clocks retain explicit shared-engine mappings. Predefined Viy, hidden operator cards and tutorial activations in17-16 remain unsupported and separately gated; operator/module/visual scope is not inferred from this enemy registration."
